<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 36,978 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 36,978 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 36,978 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday, compared to 48,643 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Tuesday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 7,783	   11,626</p>
<p>    Import cargo			29,195	   37,017</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, two ships sailed and eight berthed. In the next 24 hours six ships were expected to sail and eight were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>Feul oil		 40,000	 Al Safa	     1/10</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Wawasan Megah     3/10</p>
<p>High speed deisel    27,500	 Sand Gate	   30/9</p>
<p>High speed deisel    55,000	 Al Maqwa	     due</p>
<p>Sugar		    13,000	 Halldor	     1/10</p>
<p>High speed deisel    56,000	 Kanpolis	    8/10</p>
<p>Sugar		    12,000	 Gur Maiden	   due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
